# Line-ending contract for the LYGO LLM Console package.
#
# kit/KIT_SHA256SUMS.txt and kit/PUBLIC_KIT.json record a SHA-256 per shipped file. A hash of
# bytes changes when git rewrites line endings, so a clone made with core.autocrlf=true (the
# Windows default) and one made with core.autocrlf=false would produce two different trees --
# one of which fails verify_kit.py against the published digests. These rules make the working
# tree identical on every platform, so the digests describe the repo as well as the package.
#
# .bat/.cmd stay CRLF because cmd.exe parses them; everything else is LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
